_refine.details                                  
;USED WEIGHTED FULL MATRIX LEAST SQUARE PROCEDURE. THE DNA BASE PAIRS
1, 8 AND 15 ARE NOT PALINDROMIC. IN REFINEMENT THE CENTRAL BASE M 8
WAS MODELED USING ADENINE AND THYMINE WITH 50 % OCCUPANCY EACH,
RESPECTIVELY. BASE M 1 WAS EITHER CYTOSINE OR THYMINE AND BASE M 15
WAS EITHER GUANINE OR ADENINE. DUE TO CLOSE CRYSTAL PACKING CONTACTS
THESE TERMINAL BASES WERE FOUND DISORDERED AND WERE MODELED AS
CYTOSINE (BASE M 1) AND ADENINE (BASE M 15), RESPECTIVELY.
